When developing web applications, developers can choose between plain JavaScript or libraries and frameworks like React.js to build user interfaces.

Plain JavaScript requires direct DOM manipulation using selectors and event listeners.
UI updates and state handling in JavaScript are managed manually.
Manual DOM handling becomes complex and difficult to maintain in large-scale applications.
React.js uses a component-based architecture with JSX and the Virtual DOM for better performance and scalability.
JavaScript
JavaScript is a scripting language mainly used for web development to create dynamic and interactive web pages. It enables developers to control page behavior directly in the browser.

Allows DOM manipulation and handling of user interactions such as clicks and inputs.
It was developed by Brenden Eich in 1995.
Earlier known as Mocha and later LiveScript, and is now known simply as JavaScript.
ReactJS
ReactJS is a popular open-source JavaScript library used for building user interfaces in a structured and efficient manner. It helps developers create fast and interactive web applications.

Maintained by Facebook along with a large open-source community.
Enables creation of dynamic and user-friendly applications using reusable components.
Benefits of Choosing React over JavaScript
ReactJS provides several advantages over plain JavaScript when building dynamic and interactive web applications.

Component-Based Architecture: Breaks the UI into small, reusable components, improving reusability and scalability.
Better Code Organization and Maintenance: Modular components make applications easier to manage and maintain.
JSX Support: Allows writing HTML-like syntax within JavaScript files for more readable and declarative UI code.
Efficient DOM Manipulation: Uses a Virtual DOM to update only changed parts, improving performance and user experience.
State Management: Provides an efficient mechanism to manage and update component state.
SEO Friendly: Supports server-side rendering, making React applications more SEO-friendly than plain JavaScript apps.
Creating Web Pages Using JavaScript and ReactJS
It involves building dynamic and interactive user interfaces using plain JavaScript or the ReactJS library for better structure, performance, and scalability.

1. Using Plain JavaScript
The vanilla or plain JavaScript is run on the browser with the help of HTML. and It increases the length of code.

Example: The plain JavaScript is used to create a simple web page in the below code example.


<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <title>
        Hello World
    </title>
</head>

<body style="text-align: center;">
    <h2>
        Welcome To GFG
    </h2>
    <button id='btn'>
        Click Me!
    </button>
    <script>

        const btn = document.
            getElementById('btn');
        btn.addEventListener('click',
            () => {
                alert('Hello World!!');
            });
    </script>
</body>

</html>
